[stderr] 
[stderr] Create no more than three bounded GB writers, one per selected module, plus
[stderr] `GC0001.md`. Register each new file's normal Supervisor metadata and output
[stderr] paths. Each GB writer may create at most five focused `G####.md` tasks, and
[stderr] every G task must declare its actual `design_authoring_batch: GB####`.
[stderr] 
[stderr] For this football-trivia programme, allocate design evidence for: original
[stderr] question-card grammar and four named QB-A editorial batches with sources and
[stderr] reviews; adjudication/fairness and anti-repeat rules; First Whistle, Mixed
[stderr] Fixture, score/streak/results rules; guided accessibility, recovery/offline,
[stderr] and target parity. G tasks must create/review detailed bibles, not code and not
[stderr] implementation B/R runbooks.
[stderr] 
[stderr] `GC0001` must check G ownership, the five-G-per-GB limit, canonical GAME and
[stderr] GPI coverage, dependency closure, original-expression/provenance evidence,
[stderr] asset/audio accessibility equivalents, output quality, and manifest
[stderr] consistency. If any selected module or production entry lacks accepted detailed
[stderr] evidence, create exactly one successor `GD####` dispatcher for the next bounded
[stderr] wave. When all required evidence is accepted, create a final `GQ####` audit.
[stderr] Only that audit may update the canonical bible/inventory and set manifest
[stderr] `status: accepted`, accepted `final_audit`, accepted module entries with output
[stderr] paths/GAME IDs/GPI IDs, and empty pending/blocked arrays after running the
[stderr] dedicated manifest completion check. The implementation-coverage validator is
